<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="prep-2-19">
  <title>Resources for 2/19</title>

  <objectives>
    <introduction>
      <p>For the content of this class, you will be expected to be able to do the following:</p>
    </introduction>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          Explain the definition of the <em>composition</em> of two relations.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Relate composition of relations to composition of functions.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Given two appropriate relations, determine elements related under the composition of relations.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Prove theorems about composition of relations.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <subsection xml:id="video-activity-composition">
    <title>Video &amp; Activities for Composition of Relations</title>
    <p>
      Below is a YouTube video on <em>composition of relations</em>. It is followed by a link to a set of activities that we will be working on in class. Please watch the video and do as many of the activities as you can before class.
    </p>

    <video youtube="IZzOgiYB4o4" />

    <problem>
      <title>Composition of Relations</title>
      <p>
      For the following, let <m>E_n</m> be the relation on <m>\mathbb{Z}</m> given by <m>aE_nb</m> precisely when  <m>a \equiv b</m> (mod <m>n</m>), let <m>\mid</m> be the divisibility relation on <m>\mathbb{Z}</m>, and let <m>\le</m> be the ordinary <q>less than or equal</q> relation on any set of real numbers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <p>
              Consider the relation <m>R=E_4 \circ E_6</m>.
              <ol>
                <li>
                  <p>
                    Find some ordered pairs in this relation.
                  </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p>
                    Find all the integers <m>x</m> such that <m>3Rx</m>.
                  </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                  <p>
                    Find all the integers <m>y</m>$ such that <m>8Ry</m>.
                  </p>
                </li>
              </ol>
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              Do the same as in #1 for <m>R=E_5 \circ E_4</m>.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p>
              Do the same as in #1 for <m>R=\le \circ \mid</m>.  Also, determine all <m>z</m> such that <m>0Rz</m>.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </p>
    </problem>
  </subsection>

  <subsection>
    <title>Optional Reading</title>
    <p>
      <url href="">Composition of Relations</url>
    </p>
  </subsection>
</section>